00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.830
There isn't any lock on the door.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.440
Just wash your hands, girlie.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:49.380
With you boys, it's too quiet around here.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.540
We're overdue for a nice, juicy homicide.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.110
Not till I'm off duty.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:55.640
Why don't you keep your big mouth shut?

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.320
21st Squad Detectives Gallagher.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:04:59.860
What can I do for you, sir?

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.520
My name is Simms, Antiquette Simms. I'm an attorney. I want to see the lieutenant.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:04.520
What about?

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:07.440
I represent Carl Schneider. Your office has a warrant out for him.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.120
Schneider? That's McCloud's case. You'll have to see him about it.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.570
I asked to see the lieutenant.

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:16.840
Just a minute.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.650
Water's coming through the ceiling?

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:23.610
That's a civil action, lady. Call a lawyer.

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:27.860
There's a mouthpiece by the name of Simms outside. Carl Schneider's his client.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.000
Schneider? Come to see McCloud.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.720
- He has to see you. - All right, Senator.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:40.560
Come in, please. He's in bed.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:46.190
I'm sorry, Lieutenant. I'll wait here in your office.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.380
It's okay. What about Steiner Castle? Where is he?

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.870
He's ready to surrender himself to your personal custody.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:54.550
My custody? He's MacLeod's squeal. Each man handles his own case around here.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.680
I don't want my client to have any contact with Detective MacLeod.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.000
- Why? - Because I don't...

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.800
I don't want any rubber hose used on him.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:05.600
Counselor, how long have you been practicing law? We don't assault our prisoners.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.820
My client is not frightened of McLeod for nothing.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:12.150
What frightens your client is McLeod's record for convictions.

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.110
He never gives up on a case. That's what frightens your client.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:20.470
- When can I see McLeod? - He's too any time now. You can wait in my office.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.730
Thank you.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.350
- So? - So what?

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:34.050
So what happens to me now?

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:37.290
You wait here 'til the night card opens. It's nine o'clock. You got a lawyer?

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.520
My brother-in-law's a lawyer.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:41.940
You're allowed three calls. Call 'em.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:46.830
Gee, I hate to because he's kind of a new brother-in-law,

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:51.030
and if my sister finds out she dies, she's in the fourth month, too.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.940
Suit yourself. The court'll appoint you one.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.640
Gee, I don't know what to do.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.580
Sit down.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:23.460
- When Clive gets here, tell him I want to see him. - Yes, sir.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:34.550
- Hey, Phil. - Hello, Jim.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.430
- Jim! Oh, Jim! - I'm married!

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.480
Hey, Phil, hang on the buster for a minute, will you?

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:58.710
- What are you doing here? - I came to file a missing husband report.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:07:59.920
How long has he been missing?

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:02.100
Two days.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:11.380
Well, uh, young lady, uh, let's see what we can do for you.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:19.060
Me too, Jim.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.060
Follow that car.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.590
Well, that's Dakis' car.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:22.590
He's inside.

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:23.590
He ain't going nowhere.

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:27.780
Don't let him out of your sight.

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:45.120
I've been up all night in the cheap hotel room waiting to catch a thief.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.510
I might as well have stayed up with you.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.720
I can't sleep when you're not home.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:51.320
I hate to leave you alone, baby.

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:58.840
- See the doctor. - You see?

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:07.830
same as last time look baby we're gonna have a boy and a girl if we have to upset the whole medical

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:15.270
profession all right if you say so i say so and tonight i'm gonna take you out to dinner

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:25.940
it's a date we'll celebrate celebrate what us you and me i love you man i gotta go now

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:30.000
you go on home i'll meet you there in an hour sam got a pair for you

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.820
- Got something for me? - Here's your story.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.740
- He stole $480. - Tell him in, Arthur.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.410
Regular Jesse James. Who'd he steal it from? His mother?

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.700
- Don't belittle Arthur. - Story worth a picture?

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.000
He's not ripe yet.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:01.840
Wait for his second offense.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:04.240
Don't try running for it, Buster.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:07.180
You'd just about reach that railing and suddenly you'd put on weight.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.320
Bullets are supersonic.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:10.460
Don't worry.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:12.620
I won't.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.920
Either way, empty your pockets.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:16.750
What'd you do with the money, Arthur?

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:17.610
Spent it.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:18.230
All of it?

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:18.930
Yes.

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:20.190
Turn them inside out.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.560
When were you at the stork club?

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:24.590
Wednesday night.

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:27.150
You really make the rounds, the hotspot kid.

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:28.680
Where'd you spend last night?

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.000
In my room.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.200
I was there. Where were you under the bed?

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:33.430
I sat in the park.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:34.070
All night?

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:34.570
Yes.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:35.130
It rained.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:35.810
I saw it rain.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:37.820
I didn't notice.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:38.730
Sit down.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:40.390
Roll up your sleeves.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.130
The identifying marks and the scars.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:50.350
J-O-Y.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:51.590
Who's Joy?

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:52.750
A girl.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:53.650
Your girl?

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:54.190
No.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:55.120
Who's girl?

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.040
What difference does it make?

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:57.240
I stole the money, I admit it.

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:58.390
Here's Joy again.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:00.000
Joy Carmichael.

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:06.730
Why drag her into this? She doesn't know anything about it.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.850
You wouldn't lie to me, would you, Arthur?

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:10.560
Why should I lie?

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.550
I don't know. Why should you steal?

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:18.650
Is this Joy Carmichael? Your sister?

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:23.160
Will you ask Joy to come down to the 21st Precinct Police Station right away?

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.490
Her boyfriend, Arthur Kindred, has been arrested.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:30.000
Just have her ask for Detective MacLeod.

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:33.020
- Mr. McLeod? - Yes, sir.

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:40.030
- Come in here. - Hey, Red.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:42.420
- This is Detective McLeod, Mr. Sims. - How do you do?

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.280
- He's an attorney. - And very clever. I've seen him in court.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:49.340
He represents Carl Schneider.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:55.280
Oh, I had the pleasure of arresting your client a year ago.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.440
So I'm informed.

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:00.000
Change his lawyer's sense, if not his business.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.280
He's a retired doctor. He has a farm in New Jersey.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.160
- With a little sideline in New York. - A very profitable one.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:09.130
- Where's your boy? - He's ready to surrender himself on the warrant you had issued.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:13.330
- Fine. Bring him in. - Before I do, I have here some photographs.

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:20.900
- Now, these were taken only an hour ago. - Nudes. Ugly, isn't he?

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:24.020
- And he's no Mr. America. - No, that he's not.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:27.240
Now, you'll observe, there are no bruises or lacerations of any kind.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:30.000
This is the way I'm delivering my client to you, and this is the way...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.880
- That's the way I want him back. - I should think that any change whatsoever would be an improvement.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:37.810
And I want you to know I'm not going to allow you to violate his constitutional rights.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:41.450
You're not to abuse him physically nor degrade his dignity as a human being. Do you understand?

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:45.520
I saw one of your client's patients last year in the morgue in a marble slab.

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:47.980
Wasn't much human left of her and very little dignity.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.180
My client was innocent of that charge. The court acquitted him.

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:52.930
Insufficient evidence. But he was guilty.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:56.460
What are you gonna do? Try the case here? Save it for the judge.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:00.000
For over a year, McCloud, you personally have been making my client

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.790
a living nightmare. Why?

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:07.800
Because I'm annoyed by criminals that get away with murder.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:09.710
- They upset me. - That's your story?

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:10.570
Yeah.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.380
I've investigated and discovered otherwise.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:13.800
- What are you driving at, Simms? - What?

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:14.920
Nothing yet.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:17.850
I vouch for every man on my squad and that goes from a cloud.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:19.350
If you got something to say, say it.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:21.270
When it serves my purpose, not before.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.690
Meanwhile, Lieutenant, I'm warning you, not a hand on my client.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.830
- What's he driving at? - A fishing expedition.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:36.340
Not without bait. He hinted you're after Schneider for personal reasons.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.800
The Anderson girl is lying in the hospital.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.560
Last year, a girl who trusted him died when her baby was born.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.120
What happened to her baby in lots of others nobody knows.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.360
That's why I take a personal interest in Schneider.

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:48.640
This is an impersonal business, MacLeod.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.760
- How many... - He's a butcher and a murderer.

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:53.570
You ought to visit his farm, especially the kitchen.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:55.530
Looks like a place where they slaughter chickens.

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:58.930
Your moral indignation is beginning to give me a quick pain in the neck.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.000
I don't like love.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:04.380
It marks my squad lousy. I don't like it, and I won't have it.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:07.380
- You understand? - Yes, sir.

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:10.380
Can't you say "yes, sir" without making it sound like an insult?

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:12.480
- Yes, sir. - You're getting too superior, McLeod.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:15.480
A one-man army against crime. What's eating you?

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:18.300
I hate criminals. I don't believe in coddling.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.700
- Who tells you to? - You do. The whole system does.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:22.700
What do you want to do? Push Schneider on a rack?

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:28.040
No. I want to put him in the electric chair where he belongs and pull a switch myself.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.800
Sometimes, McCloud, you talk like a maniac.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.400
You want to be judge and jury, too? Well, you can't do it.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:38.520
All right, look, suppose you look after Schneider yourself when he surrenders, huh?

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.480
Make sure he's comfortable, that he gets everything he wants.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.960
I'm taking my wife out to dinner tonight, and I'm going to sleep late tomorrow.

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:48.040
That's fine. Wrap up your squeals for today and get out of here.

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:52.280
- I don't want to see you for 24 hours. - You won't. Mind if I shave?

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:56.150
You gotta have the last word, don't you?

00:14:56.850 --> 00:15:00.000
- Man after me, Omar. - Hi, Joe.

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:04.490
- Here you are, girlie. - How much do I owe you?

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:09.160
- It's on the house. - That's very decent of you. I mean, very decent.

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:18.120
- Well, you didn't kill anybody. - Embezzlement. Chicken feed.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:23.140
- Yeah, kid. - I don't want 'em.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.020
Look, son, the city don't care if you go hungry here.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.710
We chip in for the stuff ourselves.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.950
- The branch of the service we're in.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.270
- Navy.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:40.420
- Which service?

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:43.870
- The marshals, Marianas, Iwo Jima.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:46.090
- My kid was in the Navy too.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.840
Juno, you know her?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.040
- She was a cruiser.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:53.040
- Yeah.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:55.300
- Didn't she go down with all hands?

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:59.410
- There were 10 survivors.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:00.000
- Rough deal.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:03.590
He'd have been just about your age.

00:16:03.590 --> 00:16:10.520
How'd you get into this mess?

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:11.860
Are you going to give me a sermon?

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:13.220
Don't get funny with me, son.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:16.410
I'll knock you right through the floor.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.820
How'd you get into this mess?

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:51.400
- Hi, Lou. - Hi, Jim.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.560
Here comes trouble.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.730
- What do you got there? - Burglars. Caught a red hen.

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:12.880
I come running down the stairs and I collared him.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.650
This one gave me a struggle.

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:16.210
I'm walking down the stairs.

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:17.710
I'm minding my own business.

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:19.130
The cock jumps on, Tommy.

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:20.590
Starts beating my brain, Tommy.

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:23.670
All right.

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:25.810
He'll come to you.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.830
Think I'm crazy doing things like this?

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:29.100
Sit down.

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:30.000
On this one we found.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.520
How about this? And this, Jimmy? Twenty-two? Loaded.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.560
What's your name? Stand up.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:40.000
Janini, Charles Janini. I don't know nothing. I don't even notice.

