00:48:17.460 --> 00:48:18.760
I should be getting first-grade money.

00:48:21.040 --> 00:48:30.000
You got one of those two-way...

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:35.870
Radio Vistwatches like to Tracy, see, Phil?

00:48:35.870 --> 00:48:37.690
- No.

00:48:37.690 --> 00:48:41.330
- You're behind the times, aren't you?

00:48:41.330 --> 00:48:45.410
Oh, I'm getting a reaction.

00:48:45.410 --> 00:48:48.290
Yeah, see, I got diabetes.

00:48:48.290 --> 00:48:51.050
I'm not supposed to get emotions, see, Phil.

00:48:51.050 --> 00:48:53.190
- Look, I got ulcers.

00:48:53.190 --> 00:48:55.210
I'm not supposed to eat sandwiches.

00:48:55.210 --> 00:48:56.170
Do me a favor.

00:48:56.170 --> 00:48:58.210
Next time, get yourself arrested before four o'clock.

00:48:58.210 --> 00:48:59.700
Let a guy eat a home-cooked meal.

00:49:00.160 --> 00:49:02.200
Do you realize this is all on my own time?

00:49:02.280 --> 00:49:03.970
Look at all these forms of how to type up.

00:49:04.000 --> 00:49:05.700
When I get to court, the judge will probably let you off.

00:49:05.780 --> 00:49:07.420
I won't even get a conviction.

00:49:07.500 --> 00:49:09.890
Yeah, you caused me all this work for nothing.

00:49:09.890 --> 00:49:13.380
- Oh, I'm sorry. - All right, go wash your hands.

00:49:13.460 --> 00:49:15.080
That's a big help.

00:49:15.290 --> 00:49:17.120
In there.

00:49:17.450 --> 00:49:23.870
Yeah? She doesn't answer?

00:49:23.950 --> 00:49:28.680
You sure? No, I'll call back later.

00:49:31.210 --> 00:49:34.440
- Yes, sir? - My name is Pritchett. Albert R. Pritchett.

00:49:34.520 --> 00:49:38.850
- Open him in, Mr. Pritchett. We've been expecting you. - Did you get my money back?

00:49:38.960 --> 00:49:41.830
- I'm afraid not. - What did he do with it?

00:49:41.890 --> 00:49:46.530
- Women, plush saloons, cabarets. I wouldn't have thought it. He seems such an honest boy.

00:49:46.610 --> 00:49:50.130
- You'll prefer charges? We can count on you. - Oh, and I make up my mind. I'm like iron.

00:49:50.210 --> 00:49:52.210
- Fine. Thank you, Mr. Pritchett. - I'm like iron.

00:49:52.290 --> 00:49:58.290
- Arthur, on your feet. Is this the boy? - Yes, I'm afraid it is.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:05.960
- Why did you steal from me? Did I treat you badly? - No, Mr. Pritchett.

00:50:05.960 --> 00:50:09.000
- Did I pay you a decent salary? - Yes.

00:50:09.000 --> 00:50:14.750
And why did you do this to me? I'd built up my business from a hole in the wall.

00:50:14.750 --> 00:50:17.790
I worked darned hard for it, and I want my money back.

00:50:17.790 --> 00:50:19.870
- And you'll get it, I promise you. - Susan.

00:50:19.870 --> 00:50:23.210
The bank was closed. All I could scrape together tonight was $120.

00:50:23.210 --> 00:50:24.710
I'll have the rest tomorrow.

00:50:24.710 --> 00:50:25.830
- Take that. - Who is this?

00:50:25.830 --> 00:50:27.670
- Don't let me alone. Don't interfere. - Who are you, miss?

00:50:27.670 --> 00:50:30.000
I'm Susan Carmichael. I'm an old friend of ours.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.000
I'd like to straighten this out with you, Mr...

00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:34.000
Pritchett. Albert R. Pritchett.

00:50:34.000 --> 00:50:35.000
How do you do, Mr. Pritchett?

00:50:35.000 --> 00:50:38.000
How do you do? You say you're prepared to return the rest of my money, young lady?

00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:40.000
Yes, I'll sign a promissory note or whatever you say.

00:50:40.000 --> 00:50:42.000
Say, where'd you get that cash, Mr. Carmichael?

00:50:42.000 --> 00:50:48.150
I had some, and I pawned some jewelry. Here are the tickets. Do you want to see them?

00:50:48.150 --> 00:50:54.360
If you don't mind. Anything of your sisters here?

00:50:54.360 --> 00:50:55.700
No.

00:50:55.700 --> 00:50:56.700
Is this the young lady who's...

00:50:56.700 --> 00:50:58.710
No. She doesn't know anything about it.

00:50:58.710 --> 00:51:00.000
I know all there is to know.

00:51:00.860 --> 00:51:04.840
- Shall I make out a note for the rest? - Wait a minute, we don't run a collection agency here.

00:51:04.840 --> 00:51:08.720
This man's a thief. We're here to prosecute criminals, not collect money.

00:51:08.720 --> 00:51:12.820
- He's not a criminal. - Miss Carmichael, you seem like a very nice young lady.

00:51:12.820 --> 00:51:17.100
I'm going to give you some advice. I've seen a thousand like them.

00:51:17.100 --> 00:51:19.380
- You take your money and run. - Cloud?

00:51:19.380 --> 00:51:22.560
- Yes, sir? - That'd be the files on the Cotsworth Squale.

00:51:22.560 --> 00:51:25.800
- Cotsworth? 1941? - Yeah.

00:51:25.800 --> 00:51:29.920
- Well, that'll be buried under a pile upstairs. I'll have to dig them up. - Dig them up?

00:51:30.160 --> 00:51:32.790
- Do it now. - Yes, sir.

00:51:33.700 --> 00:51:36.900
It spells one thing for you: misery the rest of your life.

00:51:36.980 --> 00:51:38.980
It's no good. Believe me, I know.

00:51:39.060 --> 00:51:40.310
That isn't true.

00:51:45.650 --> 00:52:00.000
Richard, he never did anything dishonest before.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:03.760
- Then why did he do it? - He had a good job. He wasn't hungry.

00:52:03.840 --> 00:52:05.380
- I was. - What?

00:52:05.460 --> 00:52:07.960
You can be hungry for other things besides food.

00:52:08.040 --> 00:52:11.260
You were very decent to me, Mr. Pritchett.

00:52:11.340 --> 00:52:14.530
You trusted me and I let you down. I'm sorry.

00:52:14.610 --> 00:52:18.540
Why did you do it, Arthur?

00:52:18.620 --> 00:52:22.000
It's hard to explain, even to myself.

00:52:22.080 --> 00:52:25.990
I'd been separated from my girl for five years.

00:52:26.070 --> 00:52:29.700
She'd moved into a new world, way out of my reach.

00:52:30.350 --> 00:52:32.660
Take her out for an evening cost two weeks of my salary.

00:52:33.230 --> 00:52:36.980
Late collections had come in. Your money was in my pocket.

00:52:37.710 --> 00:52:39.960
I didn't care about anything except holding on to her.

00:52:40.040 --> 00:52:43.540
It was my last chance. I lost anyway.

00:52:44.330 --> 00:52:46.620
- You admit you did wrong? - Of course I do.

00:52:46.740 --> 00:52:49.840
- You're willing to make restitution? - Tomorrow morning, I promise.

00:52:52.570 --> 00:52:55.700
Mr. Pritchett, this kid took a lot of chances for us.

00:52:56.260 --> 00:52:58.120
Don't you think we ought to take one for him?

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:02.330
You know, it's funny you should say that.

00:53:02.330 --> 00:53:05.330
I was talking to my brother-in-law just the other night about my nephew.

00:53:05.330 --> 00:53:07.720
I'm at exactly that point. I was saying that the only--

00:53:07.720 --> 00:53:09.220
Yes, and you were right, Mr. Pritchett.

00:53:09.220 --> 00:53:11.720
Arthur, wait outside. Sit down, Mr. Pritchett.

00:53:11.720 --> 00:53:17.200
Now, I can see that you're a man who knows his own mind, Mr. Pritchett.

00:53:17.200 --> 00:53:26.400
This way, please.

00:53:32.520 --> 00:53:34.780
- How do you do, Mr. Clarke? - What's this about, Lieutenant?

00:53:34.780 --> 00:53:37.130
- Have a seat. - Where's my husband?

00:53:37.130 --> 00:53:38.710
He'll be here in a few minutes.

00:53:38.710 --> 00:53:41.110
- He hasn't been hurt? - No, no.

00:53:41.110 --> 00:53:43.750
I had a terrible feeling that he...

00:53:43.750 --> 00:53:45.570
Nothing like that. He's all right.

00:53:45.570 --> 00:53:47.650
You're sure you're not trying to break it easy?

00:53:47.650 --> 00:53:49.770
You'll see him in a few minutes. I give you my word.

00:53:49.770 --> 00:53:57.040
- Please sit down. - Then what is it? What's wrong?

00:53:57.040 --> 00:54:00.000
The prisoner here was assaulted by your husband.

00:54:02.400 --> 00:54:04.510
- Jim wouldn't do that. - He did.

00:54:04.510 --> 00:54:06.960
This could be very serious, Mrs. McLeod.

00:54:06.960 --> 00:54:08.820
This could cost your husband his job.

00:54:08.820 --> 00:54:13.710
He could even wind up in jail.

00:54:13.710 --> 00:54:16.100
- Is there anything I can do to help? - Yes.

00:54:16.100 --> 00:54:18.480
By answering some questions, by telling me the truth.

00:54:18.480 --> 00:54:19.940
Willing to go along?

00:54:19.940 --> 00:54:22.250
Yes, of course I am.

00:54:22.250 --> 00:54:26.460
Did you ever run into a man named Carl Schneider?

00:54:26.460 --> 00:54:30.000
- No. - My cigar, I think?

00:54:30.990 --> 00:54:38.700
no did you ever hear your husband mentioned that name jim made it a rule never to discuss his work

00:54:38.700 --> 00:54:44.960
with me it took me 10 years to train my wife it's a tough life being married to a cop i don't think

00:54:44.960 --> 00:54:52.910
so i'm happy you love your husband very much when did you leave highland falls the spring of 1941 i

00:54:52.910 --> 00:55:00.000
got a job in a defense plant where in newark this doctor was practicing in newark about that time doctor

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.720
- Oh, he's a doctor? - Yeah.

00:55:02.720 --> 00:55:05.750
Never ran into him around Newark, maybe?

00:55:05.750 --> 00:55:08.400
- No, I don't know him. - Knows you?

00:55:08.400 --> 00:55:12.080
- What makes you think that? - He said so.

00:55:12.080 --> 00:55:16.920
I'm afraid he's mistaken.

00:55:16.920 --> 00:55:19.920
He was positive. Carl Schneider. Ring any bells?

00:55:19.920 --> 00:55:23.620
No, I'm afraid not.

00:55:23.620 --> 00:55:26.100
He looks away then. Why?

00:55:26.100 --> 00:55:29.670
Did I? I wasn't conscious of it.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:34.030
- Are you sure Dr. Schneider never treated you?

00:55:34.030 --> 00:55:36.140
- Certainly not.

00:55:36.140 --> 00:55:38.430
I just told you no.

00:55:38.430 --> 00:55:40.880
- Why are you so indignant?

00:55:40.880 --> 00:55:45.440
I didn't say what he treated you for.

00:55:45.440 --> 00:55:54.420
Come in.

00:55:54.420 --> 00:55:56.020
Mrs. McLeod, I'm going to have to ask you

00:55:56.020 --> 00:55:57.650
a very personal question.

00:56:00.030 --> 00:56:05.620
- Did you ever have a child? - You know Jim and I have no children.

00:56:05.640 --> 00:56:10.360
I mean, before you were married to Jim?

00:56:10.370 --> 00:56:18.890
- I was never married to anyone but Jim. - I know that.

00:56:18.950 --> 00:56:27.360
- Then how can you ask? - Mrs. McLeod, my job is to find out the truth.

00:56:27.400 --> 00:56:29.030
Please answer that question.

00:56:30.730 --> 00:56:35.050
- You have no right to ask that. - I have a right to get at the truth.

00:56:35.350 --> 00:56:40.740
- Did you ever have a baby? - No, Lieutenant Monaghan, I did not.

00:56:41.390 --> 00:56:44.090
Does this name mean anything to you?

00:56:44.240 --> 00:56:51.540
- Tammy, Jack O'Petty? - No.

00:57:21.720 --> 00:57:28.360
- What is this, Lieutenant? - Sorry, Mrs. Clark.

00:57:32.200 --> 00:57:39.250
Come, rest alive.

00:58:01.370 --> 00:58:04.290
Line on the sidewalk, huh, man or woman?

00:58:04.290 --> 00:58:07.330
Where, please? 353?

00:58:07.330 --> 00:58:10.430
353, isn't that on the north side of the street?

00:58:10.430 --> 00:58:13.240
Well, that's the 16th Precinct. Call them.

00:58:13.240 --> 00:58:15.240
Any report on Schneider yet?

00:58:15.240 --> 00:58:22.720
Say, Jim, I just had a long talk with Mr. Pritchett,

00:58:22.720 --> 00:58:25.020
and he's willing to drop the charges.

00:58:25.020 --> 00:58:27.820
He is? What's this about, Mr. Pritchett?

00:58:27.820 --> 00:58:30.000
I'd like to give the boy another chance.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:34.980
- Heal from someone else? - I wouldn't want this on my conscience.

00:58:35.060 --> 00:58:36.790
Suppose he commits a worse crime.

00:58:36.890 --> 00:58:39.090
What about your conscience then, Mr. Pritchett?

00:58:39.200 --> 00:58:41.400
I'll gamble. I'm a gambler.

00:58:41.480 --> 00:58:44.060
I bet on horses. At this once, I'll bet on a human being.

00:58:44.140 --> 00:58:46.280
You stick to horses. The percentage is better.

00:58:46.360 --> 00:58:49.340
Now, just a minute, Jim. I advise Mr. Pritchett to do this.

00:58:49.460 --> 00:58:52.820
You had no right to do that, Lou. This is my case. You know better.

00:58:52.860 --> 00:58:54.770
- I didn't think you'd mind, Jim. - Well, I do.

00:58:54.850 --> 00:58:58.400
- Well, I'm sorry. - But you said that everything would be all...

00:58:58.480 --> 00:58:59.510
I made a mistake.

00:59:00.060 --> 00:59:02.100
It's his case. The disposition of it is up to him.

00:59:02.180 --> 00:59:04.700
- Well, if everybody can say this... - I'm sorry, girl. You've got to leave me out of this.

00:59:04.780 --> 00:59:06.700
It's his case. Take it up with him.

00:59:06.930 --> 00:59:09.350
Mr. MacLeod, I'm going to return the money, and if Mr. Pritchett...

00:59:09.430 --> 00:59:12.450
Young lady, this isn't a civil case. This is a criminal action.

00:59:12.530 --> 00:59:17.600
Jim, take a look at this sheet on Charlie.

00:59:19.400 --> 00:59:21.820
One second, Mr. Pritchett.

00:59:22.020 --> 00:59:25.060
- So you didn't done it, Charlie? - No.

00:59:25.390 --> 00:59:28.280
- No, my mother is great. - And you never been in jail?

00:59:28.740 --> 00:59:30.000
Hey, I dropped it.

00:59:30.250 --> 00:59:33.480
What do you guys want from that?

00:59:33.480 --> 00:59:37.040
Breaking, isn't it?

00:59:37.040 --> 00:59:40.880
These are your fingerprints, Charlie. They never lie.

00:59:40.880 --> 00:59:45.360
Burglary and arrests, two assaults, three muggings, one rape,

00:59:45.360 --> 00:59:48.850
two homicides, five extortions, one prison break.

00:59:48.850 --> 00:59:50.530
Nice little sheep, Charlie.

00:59:50.530 --> 00:59:54.400
He's a full-time loser. If he makes one false move, hit him over the head.

00:59:54.400 --> 00:59:57.300
Book him and bring him back here for the inspector.

00:59:57.300 --> 00:59:59.920
And book that bum, too.

01:00:01.630 --> 01:00:03.360
- You got a cigarette.

01:00:03.360 --> 01:00:05.320
- What do you want, room service?

01:00:05.320 --> 01:00:08.190
- Well, it's the Green Light Hotel, ain't it?

01:00:08.190 --> 01:00:09.640
- Take 'em away.

01:00:29.210 --> 01:00:29.730
Where they land.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:35.150
They cry, but don't think it's your laughter or your tears. It isn't.

01:00:35.650 --> 01:00:38.580
They're a different breed. Believe me, I know.

01:00:39.100 --> 01:00:42.960
Who are you, God? Didn't you ever make a mistake?

01:00:43.070 --> 01:00:48.450
Yes. When I was new on this job, we brought in two boys caught stealing from a car.

01:00:48.520 --> 01:00:51.480
They looked like babies. They cried. I let them go.

01:00:51.950 --> 01:00:54.350
Two nights later, two nights,

01:00:54.600 --> 01:00:58.000
one of them held up a butcher in Harlem, shot him to the head and killed him.

01:00:58.360 --> 01:00:59.600
Yes, I made a mistake.

01:01:00.120 --> 01:01:02.160
- And I'm not gonna make it again. - But officer...

01:01:02.160 --> 01:01:04.040
Young lady, I don't want to discuss this with you.

01:01:04.040 --> 01:01:05.790
- Don't talk to her like that. - Shut up!

01:01:05.790 --> 01:01:13.370
Damn!

01:01:13.370 --> 01:01:15.900
You're dealing with a criminal of mine, Mr. Pritchett.

01:01:15.900 --> 01:01:17.910
Softness is dangerous.

01:01:17.910 --> 01:01:19.370
But if it's a first offense...

01:01:19.370 --> 01:01:22.750
It's never a first offense. It's just the first time they get caught.

01:01:22.750 --> 01:01:24.130
Why are you so vicious?

01:01:24.130 --> 01:01:30.000
I'm not vicious, young lady. I didn't steal this man's money. He did.

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:34.800
This is a war, Mr. Pritchett. We're your army. We're here to protect you.

01:01:34.800 --> 01:01:39.600
But you civilians are too lazy or selfish or scared or just too indifferent

01:01:39.600 --> 01:01:43.420
to even want to appear in court and see the charges through that you yourselves bring.

01:01:43.420 --> 01:01:47.080
- But if I get paid... - I don't care about that.

01:01:47.080 --> 01:01:50.280
This is a criminal action. Are you or aren't you going through with it

01:01:50.280 --> 01:01:52.390
because I'm not gonna let him go.

01:01:52.390 --> 01:01:56.400
- If I don't bring charges... - Then I'll book him anyway and subpoena you into court.

01:01:56.400 --> 01:02:00.000
- Oh, well... - It's my duty to protect you in spite of yourself.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:02.120
I've got to leave it up to you, officer, whatever you say.

01:02:02.160 --> 01:02:03.580
I say prosecute.

01:02:05.680 --> 01:02:08.060
All right, you know best.

01:02:10.040 --> 01:02:13.500
I'm sorry, miss, but he had no right to rob me in the first place.

01:02:13.600 --> 01:02:14.960
That was a terrible thing to do.

01:02:15.060 --> 01:02:17.620
All right, Mr. Pritchett, we won't take up any more of your time.

01:02:18.070 --> 01:02:18.960
Now, here's the address.

01:02:19.080 --> 01:02:21.020
We'll see you in court tomorrow morning at 10.

01:02:23.790 --> 01:02:28.890
There goes John Q. Puppet, a man of iron.

01:02:29.200 --> 01:02:30.000
Mr. Pritchett!

01:02:38.730 --> 01:02:43.380
Jim, the hotel is busy. He doesn't want to be disturbed.

01:03:02.940 --> 01:03:06.520
- Jim, why must you make everything so black and white?

01:03:06.520 --> 01:03:12.870
- Don't be so intolerant.

01:03:12.870 --> 01:03:14.390
I'm just trying to warn you, Jim.

01:03:14.390 --> 01:03:16.160
- What about?

01:03:16.160 --> 01:03:17.890
- You're digging your own grave.

01:03:17.890 --> 01:03:19.250
It's right there in front of you.

01:03:19.250 --> 01:03:24.100
One more step and you're in it.

01:03:24.100 --> 01:03:26.140
- Very psychic today.

01:03:26.140 --> 01:03:27.330
What's on your mind?

01:03:45.930 --> 01:03:49.270
- Come on, champ, what's this about? - Sit down, Tammy.

01:03:49.410 --> 01:03:52.120
20 buck hat. You must be rolling.

01:03:52.210 --> 01:03:54.680
40 bucks? I'm comfortable. What's on your mind, champ?

01:03:54.760 --> 01:03:57.590
- Woman, you settle, Otto. - That girl's 100%.

01:03:57.670 --> 01:04:00.000
- I won't say a thing against her. - You don't have to.

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:03.420
- She's all off the record. - When I talk, it's for the record, champ.

01:04:03.460 --> 01:04:06.760
Look, Jackopetti, I'm Lieutenant Monaghan. I'm in charge here.

01:04:06.760 --> 01:04:09.100
Keep your tongue in your mouth and we'll get along.

01:04:09.160 --> 01:04:12.390
- You mind if I call my lawyer? - It ain't necessary.

01:04:12.430 --> 01:04:17.000
- My lawyer gets mad, too. - Nothing you say. He'll be held against, you understand?

01:04:17.080 --> 01:04:19.970
- I'll give you my word. - I won't hurt that girl.

01:04:20.050 --> 01:04:22.550
I don't want you to. She's only a witness.

01:04:22.600 --> 01:04:26.340
- Sit down, Tommy. - Okay.

01:04:28.120 --> 01:04:29.890
- Shoot. - When did you know her?

01:04:31.050 --> 01:04:33.250
- Seven years ago? - You like her?

01:04:34.130 --> 01:04:38.230
I was crazy about her. She was my girl.

01:04:38.290 --> 01:04:43.750
- What broke it up? - She gave me the air.

01:04:44.290 --> 01:04:48.550
Why? Why'd she give you the air, Tommy?

01:04:49.750 --> 01:04:51.920
I think maybe I'd better call my lawyer.

01:04:51.960 --> 01:04:53.920
Look, Jacopetti, we got a sheet on you.

01:04:54.000 --> 01:04:56.340
All I got to do is lift that phone and you're out of action.

01:04:56.410 --> 01:04:59.350
- Capisce? - Capisce.

01:05:01.660 --> 01:05:04.110
Well, one day she comes to me. She's in trouble.

01:05:04.800 --> 01:05:06.650
Now I got to break it to her. I'm married.

01:05:06.900 --> 01:05:08.330
She's crying her eyes out.

01:05:08.890 --> 01:05:11.190
I'd have married her if I could have got a divorce.

01:05:12.070 --> 01:05:16.960
I'd tell her I want that kid. I'd go away with her, give her anything she wants.

01:05:17.370 --> 01:05:20.120
The moon out of the sky, I'd get it for her.

01:05:22.210 --> 01:05:25.360
Dance. Who can understand it?

01:05:26.080 --> 01:05:29.370
- Go on, Tommy. - Well, it's the last I see of it.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:33.080
Then I hear she went to some doctor. I find the place.

01:05:34.090 --> 01:05:38.290
She wouldn't see me. The baby was born dead.

01:05:40.110 --> 01:05:44.150
I had a little talk with that doctor. I beat the daylights out of him.

01:05:44.350 --> 01:05:48.280
- What was his name? - Some Dutchman, something...

01:05:48.680 --> 01:05:51.180
- Sh... Schneider? - Yeah.

01:05:51.340 --> 01:05:54.840
- Carl Schneider? - Yeah, yeah, that's it.

01:05:55.090 --> 01:05:58.240
- Thanks, Tommy. - Now, will you tell me what this is all about?

01:05:58.410 --> 01:06:00.000
- Wait. - Wait for what?

01:06:06.720 --> 01:06:16.740
- I'll have one of my men drive you home, Mrs. McLeod. - Told you, didn't he?

01:06:16.740 --> 01:06:22.610
Yes. I'm sorry I had it upset you,

01:06:22.610 --> 01:06:27.650
but Jim has been persecuting Schneider for over a year, and I had to find out why.

01:06:30.540 --> 01:06:35.640
- But Jim never knew. - Schneider's attorney says so.

01:06:36.620 --> 01:06:41.940
I don't care what he says. Jim never knew. I never told him.

01:06:43.830 --> 01:06:46.000
Mrs. McCloud, I wish I could believe you.

01:06:47.440 --> 01:06:51.920
You've got to believe me. This was my mistake. You can't punish Jim for it.

01:06:52.200 --> 01:06:55.360
If Schneider's badly hurt, the commissioner will be here, the district attorney.

01:06:55.560 --> 01:06:59.250
If that happens, I gotta have all the facts.

01:07:00.090 --> 01:07:03.880
- Lieutenant, I swear, Jim doesn't know.

01:07:03.880 --> 01:07:13.390
- That's what I have to be sure of, now.

01:07:13.390 --> 01:07:16.410
- Well?

01:07:16.410 --> 01:07:17.250
- McLeod.

01:07:17.250 --> 01:07:24.670
- Yes, sir.

01:07:24.670 --> 01:07:29.230
- Harry, trying to call you?

01:07:29.230 --> 01:07:30.000
What are you doing?

01:07:33.450 --> 01:07:37.480
- I sent for her. - Why?

01:07:38.290 --> 01:07:41.270
- That's Tammy Jacopetti. - Hi, Chan.

01:07:42.830 --> 01:07:47.210
- Say, what's this about, Lieutenant? - Schneider.

01:07:47.980 --> 01:07:51.700
- Why'd you lie to me? - I didn't lie to you.

01:07:52.090 --> 01:07:55.380
- May I please? - Go ahead.

01:07:57.180 --> 01:07:59.320
Oh, Jim.

01:08:01.370 --> 01:08:12.000
- Sit down. - What's wrong, baby?

01:08:12.000 --> 01:08:16.370
Jim, the lieutenant won't believe that you knew nothing about this.

01:08:16.370 --> 01:08:22.800
- About what, honey? - Schneider.

01:08:22.800 --> 01:08:25.990
What's he got to do with you?

01:08:30.160 --> 01:08:40.180
I had occasion to see him once.

01:08:40.180 --> 01:08:45.980
I went to him when I needed help.

01:08:45.980 --> 01:08:54.770
It was a long time ago. I was going to have a baby.

01:09:02.720 --> 01:09:07.230
It was long before I met you, Jim.

01:09:07.900 --> 01:09:19.120
I told you he didn't know.

01:09:19.200 --> 01:09:21.330
I see.

01:09:21.410 --> 01:09:24.820
Okay, diagrams aren't necessary.

01:09:24.900 --> 01:09:26.900
I get the picture. She's a good girl, Jim.

01:09:26.980 --> 01:09:30.000
- Cut that out! - I don't have to take that from you.

01:09:30.060 --> 01:09:32.140
and I'll tear your arm out of the sock.

01:09:32.150 --> 01:09:43.760
- Jim. - Mind if I talk to my wife alone?

01:09:43.800 --> 01:09:47.190
Okay, Tommy.

01:10:08.280 --> 01:10:13.080
Please forgive me.

01:10:13.080 --> 01:10:15.550
Oh, Jim, I'm terribly sorry.

01:10:15.550 --> 01:10:17.070
Please forgive me.

01:10:17.070 --> 01:10:20.300
My immaculate wife.

01:10:20.300 --> 01:10:21.580
I never said I was.

01:10:21.580 --> 01:10:24.280
You never said you weren't?

01:10:24.280 --> 01:10:26.520
Why didn't you tell me?

01:10:26.520 --> 01:10:30.000
I wanted to, but I was so afraid of losing you.

01:10:31.630 --> 01:10:35.300
- How long did you go with him? - A few months.

01:10:35.380 --> 01:10:38.820
- How many? - About six or seven.

01:10:38.900 --> 01:10:42.650
- Seven isn't a few. - No, I suppose not.

01:10:43.000 --> 01:10:46.750
- Did he give you money? - No.

01:10:47.150 --> 01:10:51.220
- Did he give you presents? - Yes, he gave me some presents.

01:10:51.300 --> 01:10:53.660
- Expensive ones? - I don't know.

01:10:53.740 --> 01:10:56.870
- What do you mean, you don't know? - I don't know.

01:10:56.950 --> 01:11:00.000
What difference does it make?

01:11:00.280 --> 01:11:03.320
This difference. I just assumed Schneider died.

01:11:03.470 --> 01:11:08.310
I'd rather go to jail for 20 years than find out my wife was a tramp.

01:11:09.090 --> 01:11:13.570
Don't say that, Jim.

01:11:14.960 --> 01:11:17.510
That's the word. I didn't invent it. That's what they call it.

01:11:20.940 --> 01:11:25.040
I don't care about they. I only care about you, Jim.

01:11:25.240 --> 01:11:27.560
And it isn't true. You know it isn't true.

01:11:31.310 --> 01:11:32.530
I thought I knew you.

01:11:33.470 --> 01:11:36.010
I thought you were everything good and pure.

01:11:40.890 --> 01:11:46.420
Judge me, Jim.

01:11:47.000 --> 01:11:48.160
I don't understand.

01:11:49.450 --> 01:11:53.030
I was on my own for the first time in a large city.

01:11:53.210 --> 01:11:54.810
The war was on.

01:11:56.060 --> 01:11:59.240
I'd only been out with kids my own age until I met this man.

01:12:00.700 --> 01:12:08.690
paid me a lot of attention. I was flattered. I thought he was romantic and glamorous. I thought

01:12:08.690 --> 01:12:30.000
I was in love with him. What happened to the child? Died at birth. Well, you can't have any children.

01:12:34.090 --> 01:12:40.550
- Oh, Jim, I take much more of this.

01:12:40.550 --> 01:12:45.290
Please try and understand.

01:12:45.290 --> 01:12:48.890
- What's there to understand?

01:12:48.890 --> 01:12:52.030
You went with a pig like that.

01:12:52.030 --> 01:12:53.950
You had a child by him.

01:12:53.950 --> 01:12:55.970
Then you went to that butcher, Schneider.

01:12:55.970 --> 01:12:58.650
Everything I ate.

01:12:58.650 --> 01:13:00.000
What's left to understand?

01:13:15.900 --> 01:13:19.030
Just got word from the hospital. Schneider's okay.

01:13:19.030 --> 01:13:28.420
- Thanks. - Sorry, Jim.

01:14:20.160 --> 01:14:22.030
- You don't look like a detective.

01:14:22.030 --> 01:14:23.390
- No?

01:14:23.390 --> 01:14:26.450
What's a detective look like?

01:14:26.450 --> 01:14:30.000
- They wear derbies.

01:14:31.980 --> 01:14:33.820
- You're a nice looking fella. - Thanks.

01:14:33.820 --> 01:14:37.480
- You married? - Yeah.

01:14:37.480 --> 01:14:39.380
Yeah.

01:15:14.400 --> 01:15:24.390
- Quick, eyes. - He's off.

01:15:30.380 --> 01:15:32.310
You might as well go home now, young lady.

01:15:32.310 --> 01:15:35.040
As soon as we print him, I'm through.

01:15:35.040 --> 01:15:49.710
All right, Arthur, over there.

01:15:49.710 --> 01:15:55.320
Don't hurt.

01:15:55.320 --> 01:15:57.770
Don't hurt, you roll it like that.

01:15:57.770 --> 01:16:00.000
It gets your hands a little dirty, you wash it.

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:16.460
right off. It's nothing. What's the matter? Did I say something? You Mavvy? Me neither.

01:16:18.720 --> 01:16:23.680
Everybody tells you, why don't you get Mavvy? You should be Mavvy. My mother, my father,

01:16:23.800 --> 01:16:29.030
my sisters. I ain't get Mavvy. As if I didn't want to get Mavvy.

01:16:30.510 --> 01:16:32.470
Where do you find a man?

01:16:32.780 --> 01:16:37.720
You get me a man and I'll mabby him. Anything, as long as it's got pants.

01:16:39.160 --> 01:16:45.010
Get mabby. It's easy to talk.

01:16:52.630 --> 01:17:00.000
Dolly, did you boy glorize this?

01:17:00.030 --> 01:17:04.520
Why don't you give us a break?

01:17:04.520 --> 01:17:06.640
You do us a favor, we might help you.

01:17:06.640 --> 01:17:09.860
How are you gonna help me?

01:17:09.860 --> 01:17:12.850
I'm a four-time loser. I'm going to jail the rest of my life.

01:17:12.850 --> 01:17:15.700
How are you gonna help me, eh?

01:17:15.700 --> 01:17:18.390
You lived a louse. You want to die a louse?

01:17:18.390 --> 01:17:22.030
Yeah. Remember, the sign says "courtesy."

01:17:22.030 --> 01:17:26.030
Courtesy? For you? You want courtesy?

01:17:26.030 --> 01:17:30.000
Hey.

01:17:32.910 --> 01:17:37.170
- I'm always squad, Detective Callahan speaking. - Yeah.

01:17:37.170 --> 01:17:39.460
Okay, Barnes, get him on here.

01:17:39.460 --> 01:17:43.460
All right, Charlie, rise and shine. You too, Lewis. Over here.

01:17:43.460 --> 01:17:46.430
- What's your first name, Barnes? - Steve.

01:17:46.430 --> 01:17:48.980
How long you been in the jail, Steve?

01:17:48.980 --> 01:17:51.370
Six years. Marry.

01:17:51.370 --> 01:17:57.910
- You louse. - Me? Thanks, I get...

01:17:57.910 --> 01:18:00.000
- 30 grand, huh? - 30 grand.

01:18:00.440 --> 01:18:04.240
- I saw the list, who do you believe, me or them?

01:18:04.240 --> 01:18:05.480
- No talking.

01:18:09.890 --> 01:18:10.840
- Them.

01:18:10.840 --> 01:18:11.540
- Quiet.

01:18:11.540 --> 01:18:16.080
You wanna spoil the picture?

01:18:16.080 --> 01:18:17.730
Okay, you two, over there.

01:18:30.410 --> 01:18:35.750
Get it on me for your protection?

01:18:35.750 --> 01:18:39.440
If this flatfoot had any sense, he's supposed to take it and let us go.

01:18:39.440 --> 01:18:41.290
Dumb cop, can I help it?

01:18:42.230 --> 01:18:45.850
Now look, I want my share.

01:18:45.850 --> 01:18:46.850
Of course.

01:18:46.850 --> 01:18:52.980
Make you happy, you're gonna have to haul $1,400.

01:18:52.980 --> 01:18:53.980
Satisfied?

01:18:53.980 --> 01:18:55.920
Yeah.

01:19:13.690 --> 01:19:15.980
Sign this.

01:19:15.980 --> 01:19:16.980
Shouldn't he see a lawyer first?

01:19:16.980 --> 01:19:17.980
Routine.

01:19:17.980 --> 01:19:18.800
On the floor.

01:19:18.800 --> 01:19:20.200
Step on it.

01:19:20.200 --> 01:19:23.240
Service.

01:19:23.240 --> 01:19:26.490
You want to be in this?

01:19:26.490 --> 01:19:28.690
Ask him, Joe.

01:19:31.820 --> 01:19:37.170
- Hey, you. - In the papers, are you?

01:19:37.370 --> 01:19:40.450
- It's all right, Susie. - I don't care.

01:19:40.490 --> 01:19:42.330
Over there, are they?

01:19:44.170 --> 01:19:46.930
Might as well go home now, young lady. It's all over.

01:19:48.370 --> 01:19:51.170
May I talk to Arthur for two minutes alone, please?

01:19:51.310 --> 01:19:53.880
- What for? - He wouldn't understand.

01:19:54.940 --> 01:19:59.350
No, I guess not. All right.

01:20:24.030 --> 01:20:25.960
Okay, quarter to nine. Let's go.

01:20:25.960 --> 01:20:28.170
Our court will be open by the time we get there.

01:20:28.170 --> 01:20:30.000
What do I do?

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:31.500
I'll tell you what to do.

01:20:31.500 --> 01:20:33.000
Your brother-in-law's gonna be there, ain't he?

01:20:33.000 --> 01:20:34.950
Yeah.

01:20:34.950 --> 01:20:42.230
All I can do is thank goodness my sister's sexy.

01:20:42.230 --> 01:20:44.850
So long, everybody.

01:20:44.850 --> 01:20:51.110
Very nice meeting you.

01:20:51.110 --> 01:20:53.080
I mean it. Very nice.

01:20:53.080 --> 01:20:55.190
Sorry if I caused you any trouble.

01:20:55.190 --> 01:20:59.530
Bye.

01:21:11.580 --> 01:21:13.000
Arthur, do you want to see Joy?

01:21:13.000 --> 01:21:15.600
Would that help? Would you like to talk to her?

01:21:15.600 --> 01:21:18.120
- No. - I'll go and get her and bring her here.

01:21:18.120 --> 01:21:20.620
I don't want her, Susie.

01:21:20.620 --> 01:21:24.080
For five years, I've been in love with a girl that doesn't exist.

01:21:24.080 --> 01:21:27.490
That's finished, washed up.

01:21:31.400 --> 01:21:34.210
Why couldn't you have fallen in love with me?

01:21:35.420 --> 01:21:37.240
I'd have been so much better for you.

01:21:38.540 --> 01:21:40.650
I've always loved you, Susie.

01:21:40.960 --> 01:21:42.510
Always my baby.

01:21:44.640 --> 01:21:45.910
I've got news for you.

01:21:46.330 --> 01:21:48.580
I voted for the president in the last election.

01:21:48.720 --> 01:21:50.340
I'm years past the age of consent.

01:21:50.690 --> 01:21:52.310
Just an old bag.

01:21:53.310 --> 01:21:55.580
Beautiful as joy is.

01:21:55.580 --> 01:21:56.040
But you are.

01:21:58.370 --> 01:21:59.830
Joy's prettier than you, but...

01:22:01.370 --> 01:22:02.250
You're more beautiful.

01:22:06.140 --> 01:22:07.440
Be my sensible, Susan.

01:22:07.640 --> 01:22:09.430
I can't be sensible about you.

01:22:09.610 --> 01:22:10.390
I love you.

01:22:34.320 --> 01:22:35.940
He's facing five to ten.

01:22:36.810 --> 01:22:39.210
Wait till the boys stop wising him up.

01:22:39.720 --> 01:22:41.580
Hey, what makes you think you'll want you to earn?

01:22:41.780 --> 01:22:42.320
Shut up.

01:22:42.940 --> 01:22:46.470
You keep coming back for a second rap or a third rap.

01:22:47.070 --> 01:22:49.230
And then you'll be a four-time loser like me.

01:22:49.470 --> 01:22:50.410
Shut up, I tell you.

01:22:50.830 --> 01:22:51.910
Look at Lewis here.

01:22:52.110 --> 01:22:53.930
That's you five years from now.

01:22:54.150 --> 01:22:54.810
Ain't it, Lewis?

01:22:55.120 --> 01:22:55.760
Shut up!

01:22:58.880 --> 01:23:00.000
Get out, Arthur.

01:23:01.690 --> 01:23:05.410
Why don't you shut up?

01:23:05.410 --> 01:23:13.100
Now, take it easy.

01:23:13.100 --> 01:23:14.810
He's not convicted yet.

01:23:14.810 --> 01:23:16.410
The judge might put him on probation.

01:23:16.410 --> 01:23:17.570
A lot of things might happen.

01:23:17.570 --> 01:23:19.800
Yeah, yeah.

01:23:19.800 --> 01:23:27.670
One more peep out of you, one, lawyer.

01:23:30.440 --> 01:23:32.530
I'm not supposed to do this, but I'll call him myself.

01:23:32.530 --> 01:23:43.480
Here's your picture, hide it from your kids.

01:24:09.370 --> 01:24:11.530
- We've been partners about eight years now, Jim.

01:24:11.530 --> 01:24:13.780
Can I ever ask you for a favor?

01:24:13.780 --> 01:24:15.190
- What is it, Lou?

01:24:15.190 --> 01:24:17.290
- That kid downstairs.

01:24:17.290 --> 01:24:18.940
I want you to give him a break.

01:24:18.940 --> 01:24:25.810
- I can't do it, Lou.

01:24:25.810 --> 01:24:28.300
- He reminds me of my boy.

01:24:28.300 --> 01:24:30.000
- Mike?

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:32.300
- He was a hero. - Why? Because he was killed?

01:24:32.310 --> 01:24:36.600
If Mike were alive today, he'd have the same problems this kid has. What do you say?

01:24:36.660 --> 01:24:41.360
- Don't ask me, will you, Lou? - But I am asking you.

01:24:41.430 --> 01:24:46.240
- No, Lou, no dice. - Louder, please. I can't seem to hear you so good.

01:24:46.320 --> 01:24:50.280
- I can't drop the charge. - Jim, this is me, Lou Brody. Remember me?

01:24:50.360 --> 01:24:53.700
What do you mean, you can't drop the charge? Mr. Pritchett left it up to you.

01:24:53.780 --> 01:24:56.960
- I can't start compromising now. - Compromise?

01:24:56.980 --> 01:25:00.000
Heart, Jim, heart. The world's crying for a little heart.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:05.430
- You shouldn't drink so much. It melts the lining of your brain. - Maybe that's what you need.

01:25:05.430 --> 01:25:08.890
Maybe it would melt that rock you've got for a heart.

01:25:08.890 --> 01:25:11.870
- Lay off, will you? - My partner. Arrest his own mother.

01:25:11.870 --> 01:25:18.790
- Lay off! I'm warning you! - What's the matter, Jim?

01:25:18.790 --> 01:25:28.640
I'm drowning. Drowning in my own juice.

01:25:31.050 --> 01:25:32.720
I wish I could understand you.

01:25:32.720 --> 01:25:34.390
I don't expect you to.

01:25:34.390 --> 01:25:36.640
I know I'm different from the others.

01:25:36.640 --> 01:25:38.110
I'm here out of principle.

01:25:38.110 --> 01:25:42.980
All my life I've lived according to principle and I couldn't change.

01:25:42.980 --> 01:25:44.660
Even if I wanted to.

01:25:44.660 --> 01:25:54.890
Jim, you gotta bend with the wind.

01:25:54.890 --> 01:25:56.060
Or break.

01:25:56.060 --> 01:25:57.720
Don't be such a monument.

01:25:57.720 --> 01:25:59.410
How?

01:26:00.440 --> 01:26:05.730
- How? - How do you compromise?

01:26:06.800 --> 01:26:09.560
I hate softness. My mother was soft that killed her.

01:26:09.640 --> 01:26:11.900
I don't believe in turning the other cheek.

01:26:13.440 --> 01:26:16.340
You asked me to compromise on this kid, who's he?

01:26:16.470 --> 01:26:18.990
Now, right now, I'm faced with a problem my own, Lou,

01:26:19.070 --> 01:26:22.720
that's ripping my guts out, and I can't compromise on that, so what do I do?

01:26:30.280 --> 01:26:34.170
- Here's your aspirin. - Listening at keyholes, Joe?

01:26:34.170 --> 01:26:40.120
I don't have to. I've had that story for a long time.

01:26:40.120 --> 01:26:47.940
She's one in a million, your Mary. She loves you. You don't know how lucky you are.

01:26:47.940 --> 01:26:53.260
- She brought warmth and tenderness into your life. - I know.

01:26:53.260 --> 01:26:56.110
- I know better than you do. - Well, then go to her.

01:26:56.110 --> 01:26:58.450
Get down on your knees and crawl.

01:27:04.920 --> 01:27:06.180
He's downstairs, Jim.

01:27:30.160 --> 01:27:38.700
Where are the keys?

01:27:38.700 --> 01:27:39.700
Inside.

01:27:39.700 --> 01:27:40.700
My taxi's waiting.

01:27:40.700 --> 01:27:41.700
You'll send it away.

01:27:41.700 --> 01:27:43.970
No, my things are in it.

01:27:43.970 --> 01:27:45.430
What things?

01:27:45.430 --> 01:27:47.670
My bags and my trunk.

01:27:47.670 --> 01:27:55.500
Please come inside.

01:27:55.500 --> 01:27:57.500
I can't talk to you here.

01:27:57.500 --> 01:27:59.060
The meter's running.

01:27:59.060 --> 01:28:00.000
Let it run.

01:28:22.140 --> 01:28:25.600
Mary, this isn't the time or place to discuss our lives.

01:28:25.890 --> 01:28:28.320
Let's go home and work this out there.

01:28:28.400 --> 01:28:29.570
You think we can?

01:28:30.920 --> 01:28:34.900
- We'll have to. - I don't. I don't think it's possible.

01:28:34.940 --> 01:28:38.040
Wait a minute. I don't get this. What are you so bitter about?

01:28:38.260 --> 01:28:40.240
Who's to blame for what happened tonight?

01:28:40.620 --> 01:28:43.740
You put me through a cement mixer. Now you're acting as if I were the...

01:28:43.820 --> 01:28:47.190
- The tramp. - Don't say that.

01:28:47.320 --> 01:28:49.720
I didn't invent the word either, Jim.

01:28:51.170 --> 01:28:57.520
- I wasn't myself. - You were never more yourself.

01:29:00.480 --> 01:29:02.360
I've thought everything over and over again.

01:29:02.820 --> 01:29:04.480
I don't see any other way out.

01:29:05.340 --> 01:29:06.520
We couldn't go on from here.

01:29:06.640 --> 01:29:08.720
Stop that kind of talk, will you, Mary?

01:29:08.720 --> 01:29:12.010
I'm trying. I'm trying.

01:29:12.130 --> 01:29:12.570
To what?

01:29:12.690 --> 01:29:13.890
To put all this behind me.

01:29:13.930 --> 01:29:14.730
Then you can't do it.

01:29:14.750 --> 01:29:15.630
If you'll let me.

01:29:16.390 --> 01:29:18.330
Now, the rest of our lives we'll be living with this.

01:29:19.400 --> 01:29:21.560
If you won't be saying it, you'll be thinking it.

01:29:22.520 --> 01:29:24.450
I couldn't take it.

01:29:25.740 --> 01:29:28.260
I'd just dry up.

01:29:33.710 --> 01:29:37.620
- Please, I'm so tired. Let me go now. - To what?

01:29:37.620 --> 01:29:39.850
- Please, Jim. - Where do you go?

01:29:39.850 --> 01:29:43.340
You turn on every light in the house when I'm not there?

01:29:43.340 --> 01:29:46.100
You can't fall asleep unless my arm's around.

01:29:46.100 --> 01:29:50.820
- Stop it. - No. I'm not gonna let you go.

01:29:50.820 --> 01:30:00.000
- Jim, you're hurting me. - Sorry. I'm sorry.

01:30:00.160 --> 01:30:02.950
Mary, but you just don't stop loving someone.

01:30:02.950 --> 01:30:11.390
I need you. Don't leave me. I love you.

01:30:11.390 --> 01:30:18.760
Help me. Help me, too.

01:30:18.760 --> 01:30:30.000
It's no use, baby. I couldn't go home if you weren't waiting.

01:30:32.080 --> 01:30:37.020
- I'd blow my brains out. - I would, Mary.

01:30:37.840 --> 01:30:40.880
If I went home to an empty flat, I wouldn't dare take my gun with me.

01:30:46.460 --> 01:30:51.860
Yeah, uh-huh.

01:30:52.310 --> 01:30:54.730
Well, his lawyer's here now, waiting to find out.

01:30:55.370 --> 01:30:56.640
All right, I'll hang on.

01:30:56.760 --> 01:30:59.600
- Where's McLeod now? - Huh? Oh.

01:31:00.060 --> 01:31:02.020
Well, uh, he... Huh?

01:31:02.020 --> 01:31:05.110
Yeah. Okay.

01:31:05.110 --> 01:31:07.750
I bring the Schneider in at 10 o'clock in the morning to book him.

01:31:07.750 --> 01:31:09.290
You can see him at the hospital after night.

01:31:09.290 --> 01:31:10.750
All right, I'll go over there.

01:31:10.750 --> 01:31:14.300
- Just a minute, McLeod. - Some other time, Counselor.

01:31:14.300 --> 01:31:17.410
No, now. They're bringing Schneider back here tomorrow.

01:31:17.410 --> 01:31:20.410
Then advise him again to keep his mouth shut and see that he does.

01:31:20.410 --> 01:31:22.410
I'm gonna break you from the force.

01:31:22.410 --> 01:31:24.360
If the last thing I do, you're gonna pay for this.

01:31:24.360 --> 01:31:28.170
How much was Miss Hatch pay?

01:31:28.170 --> 01:31:30.000
Why don't you clean up your own house?

01:31:31.280 --> 01:31:33.040
before you start to throw stones.

01:31:33.080 --> 01:31:45.570
- What do you mean by that? - You know what I mean.

01:31:45.590 --> 01:32:00.000
No, I don't know what you mean.

01:32:02.080 --> 01:32:05.380
Don't you?

01:32:32.680 --> 01:32:40.670
- What's the matter, dear? - Nothing.

01:32:40.670 --> 01:32:43.250
- It's been a horrible day. - Yes.

01:32:43.250 --> 01:32:47.520
I'm sorry, darling, and yet I'm glad it's out in the open.

01:32:47.520 --> 01:32:51.010
I've had such a terrible feeling of guilt all the time.

01:32:51.010 --> 01:32:53.110
Why? Why?

01:32:53.110 --> 01:32:58.390
I needed help, and there was no one. I... I couldn't even go to my parents.

01:33:01.050 --> 01:33:05.380
- You didn't tell them? - No, I... I didn't want to hurt them.

01:33:06.330 --> 01:33:14.800
- You know how sweet and simple they are. - You didn't go home, then?

01:33:15.600 --> 01:33:17.930
- After? - No.

01:33:19.070 --> 01:33:22.210
- Where'd you go? - I came to New York.

01:33:23.510 --> 01:33:26.400
- How long was that before I met you? - Two years.

01:33:27.950 --> 01:33:29.380
Who'd you go with then?

01:33:31.690 --> 01:33:35.090
- No one. - How many others were there married?

01:33:35.120 --> 01:33:39.910
- Others? - How many other men?

01:33:39.990 --> 01:33:44.680
- None. What's the matter with you, Jim? - Hold on a minute.

01:33:44.690 --> 01:33:49.830
- Wait a minute. - No! What's the matter with you?

01:33:49.910 --> 01:33:55.530
I had an autopsy the other day. I watched a medical exam.

01:33:55.610 --> 01:34:00.000
I saw off the top of a man's skull take out the brain and hold it in his hand.

01:34:01.470 --> 01:34:04.900
- Like that. - Why are you telling me this?

01:34:05.520 --> 01:34:08.840
'Cause I'd give my soul to take out my brain.

01:34:08.920 --> 01:34:12.080
Hold it under the faucet and wash away...

01:34:12.400 --> 01:34:15.430
the dirty pictures you've put there tonight.

01:34:15.550 --> 01:34:18.140
- Dirty pictures? - Yes.

01:34:18.180 --> 01:34:21.380
Oh, I see.

01:34:33.230 --> 01:34:38.810
Yes. Be fine.

01:34:38.810 --> 01:34:47.990
Push away what I may have put there.

01:34:47.990 --> 01:34:51.930
You'll find you're a rotten spot in your brain, Jim.

01:34:51.930 --> 01:34:54.930
And it's growing. I know I've watched it.

01:34:54.930 --> 01:34:55.930
Mary, that's enough.

01:34:55.930 --> 01:34:57.930
No, let's have the truth.

01:34:57.930 --> 01:35:00.000
I could never find it in me to say it.

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:03.040
I see tiny flaws in you, because I loved you.

01:35:03.140 --> 01:35:04.960
Oh, I still do.

01:35:05.060 --> 01:35:06.950
But let's have the truth for once.

01:35:07.910 --> 01:35:10.160
You think you're on the side of the angels.

01:35:10.230 --> 01:35:11.500
Well, you're not.

01:35:11.600 --> 01:35:16.520
You haven't even a drop of ordinary human forgiveness in your whole nature.

01:35:16.620 --> 01:35:19.890
You're a cruel and vengeful man.

01:35:20.120 --> 01:35:22.920
Everything you always said you hated in your own father.

01:35:32.460 --> 01:35:33.770
- I'm takin' you home now.

01:35:33.770 --> 01:35:34.780
- What for?

01:35:34.780 --> 01:35:44.580
So you can drive me to a lunatic asylum?

01:35:44.580 --> 01:35:47.820
- Where you going?

01:35:47.820 --> 01:35:49.680
- Goodbye, Jim.

01:35:49.680 --> 01:35:52.490
- When will I see you?

01:35:52.490 --> 01:35:53.070
- Never.

01:36:12.000 --> 01:36:14.090
There's nothing doing here.

01:36:14.090 --> 01:36:25.660
I'll go down a night court and see if I can pick up anything there.

01:36:25.660 --> 01:36:29.220
-Make out. -Fine.

01:36:30.160 --> 01:36:31.740
- I mean, Mary. - Fine. Damn it.

01:36:31.740 --> 01:36:33.920
All right, young lady. Your two minutes are up.

01:36:33.920 --> 01:36:35.540
- What's the matter with you? - Nothing.

01:36:35.540 --> 01:36:37.760
- Don't you feel well? - Yes, sir. I feel all right.

01:36:37.760 --> 01:36:40.540
- You'd better go home. - I got a squeal to finish off.

01:36:40.540 --> 01:36:43.500
- Brody, finish it off. - I'd rather do it myself.

01:36:43.500 --> 01:36:49.940
You go home. That's an order.

01:36:49.940 --> 01:36:55.130
What happened, Jim? What's wrong?

01:36:55.130 --> 01:36:58.890
- Mary left me. - She'll come back.

01:37:02.490 --> 01:37:08.910
You're finished.

01:37:08.910 --> 01:37:09.860
Drove her away, didn't you?

01:37:09.860 --> 01:37:12.350
Why?

01:37:12.350 --> 01:37:13.350
Warn you, you fool?

01:37:13.350 --> 01:37:14.400
Why?

01:37:14.400 --> 01:37:15.260
I don't know.

01:37:15.260 --> 01:37:17.920
Why do we do these things, Joe?

01:37:17.920 --> 01:37:18.920
Who knows?

01:37:18.920 --> 01:37:23.250
I built my whole life on hating my father.

01:37:23.250 --> 01:37:30.000
All the time he was inside me laughing.

01:37:30.090 --> 01:37:34.950
he was crying, or maybe he couldn't help himself either.

01:38:00.060 --> 01:38:01.060
Did you see who did it?

01:38:01.060 --> 01:38:03.560
No, I was walking on the street and someone grabbed it right out of my hand.

01:38:03.560 --> 01:38:05.560
It was so crowded I couldn't see him.

01:38:05.560 --> 01:38:08.170
- Did you have much money in it? - About $10.

01:38:08.170 --> 01:38:09.670
Must have a description.

01:38:09.670 --> 01:38:11.570
Well, it was about...

01:38:11.570 --> 01:38:12.650
Drop it! Drop it!

01:38:12.650 --> 01:38:13.650
Drop it!

01:38:13.650 --> 01:38:15.620
Drop it, boys. It's a four-time loser. We'll kill you.

01:38:15.620 --> 01:38:21.670
Rotten jail the rest of my life. I take five or six of you coppers with me first.

01:38:21.670 --> 01:38:24.670
Take it easy. You can't get by the downstairs desk.

01:38:24.670 --> 01:38:27.480
One word, one move, anyway.

01:38:31.310 --> 01:38:34.200
I was wondering when you'd get around to it, Charlie.

01:38:34.200 --> 01:38:42.390
- None of your goth. - That goth.

01:38:42.390 --> 01:38:43.740
I got you'll get it.

01:38:43.740 --> 01:38:45.730
One step, I'm warning you on!

01:38:45.730 --> 01:38:47.730
Easy, Jim, he can't get by the desk.

01:38:47.730 --> 01:38:55.550
Jim, don't be a fool!

01:38:55.550 --> 01:38:57.430
Sneaking evil.

01:39:15.040 --> 01:39:20.710
- Jim? - You gotta lie down, Jim.

01:39:21.040 --> 01:39:24.320
What's that lie down if I'm not getting up?

01:39:24.400 --> 01:39:27.870
- Get an ambulance, quick. - Never mind the doctor.

01:39:30.000 --> 01:39:33.940
- You're the priest. - You feel that bad, Jim?

01:39:36.110 --> 01:39:40.490
- St. Vincent's rectory. - Get me a drink.

01:39:41.210 --> 01:39:43.420
- Belly wound? - What difference does it make?

01:39:43.580 --> 01:39:46.620
- I don't have it. - Don't whisper, Lou.

01:39:47.200 --> 01:39:49.600
- I can hear you. - Sure you can, Jim.

01:39:49.930 --> 01:39:51.930
You're gonna be okay. They can't hurt you.

01:39:52.010 --> 01:39:56.560
- Give me a hand. Squeeze. - Send the priest over to the 21st.

01:39:56.820 --> 01:39:59.000
- Had it. - Minutes to the last rights.

01:40:09.630 --> 01:40:14.260
Give me Buster's Prince.

01:40:14.260 --> 01:40:17.310
Maybe you're right, Lou, I don't know any more.

01:40:17.310 --> 01:40:18.720
Give me his Prince.

01:40:18.720 --> 01:40:22.210
You jump.

01:40:22.210 --> 01:40:29.570
Joe, ask her to forgive me.

01:40:31.790 --> 01:40:33.840
- She needs help. - Sure.

01:40:34.150 --> 01:40:36.980
I'll take it easy.

01:40:40.810 --> 01:40:47.570
Tear 'em up, Lou. Unchain 'em.

01:40:47.690 --> 01:40:49.330
The key's in my pocket.

01:40:51.340 --> 01:40:55.090
There's no case here, Lieutenant. The complainant withdrew.

01:40:55.920 --> 01:41:00.000
Oh, Mary.

01:41:00.570 --> 01:41:15.700
Oh my God, I am hardly sorry for having offended thee.

01:41:16.650 --> 01:41:22.620
And I detest all my sins because I dread the loss of heaven and the pains of hell.

01:41:36.360 --> 01:41:39.630
but most of all, for having offended thee, my Lord,

01:41:40.930 --> 01:41:42.810
who art all good and deserving of all my love,

01:41:44.910 --> 01:41:47.010
that I firmly resolve for the help of thy grace

01:41:47.010 --> 01:41:54.530
to confess my sins, to do penance, and to amend my life.

01:41:56.000 --> 01:41:56.320
Amen.

01:42:14.750 --> 01:42:19.590
All right, son. Go on home. Don't make a monkey out of me.

01:42:20.990 --> 01:42:25.210
If I see you up here again, I'll kick the guts out of you.

01:42:26.160 --> 01:42:29.440
- Don't make a monkey out of me. - Don't worry, I won't.

01:42:30.890 --> 01:42:34.320
- He won't. - All right, go on, get out of here.

01:42:36.120 --> 01:42:39.760
I made a telegraph to you.

01:42:39.760 --> 01:42:47.660
- Get this, Harv. - Notify the commissioner.

01:42:47.740 --> 01:42:51.060
- Detector first grade James McCloud, 21st squad. - Mr. Batoni.

01:42:51.510 --> 01:42:53.720
Shot and killed in the line of duty.
